WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.426
Dr. John Dolittle lived in a small town called Puddleby.

2
00:00:05.427 --> 00:00:08.034
The townspeople knew him well.

3
00:00:08.035 --> 00:00:14.036
Dr. Dolittle looked after sick people and gave them medicine.

4
00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:16.776
Dr. Dolittle had many pets.

5
00:00:16.777 --> 00:00:19.003
Mice lived in the piano.

6
00:00:19.004 --> 00:00:21.615
He kept a squirrel in the closet.

7
00:00:21.616 --> 00:00:31.590
He also had rabbits, a very old horse, chickens, pigeons, lambs, and even a hedgehog in the basement.

8
00:00:31.591 --> 00:00:35.434
Sarah, the doctor’s sister, was his housekeeper.

9
00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:39.232
She did not like having so many animals around.

10
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.305
They made the house messy.

11
00:00:43.306 --> 00:00:46.701
Even his patients were not happy.

12
00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:50.434
"Oh, Dr. Dolittle, my knees hurt again,"

13
00:00:50.435 --> 00:00:55.059
Mrs. Keebler whined as she slowly sat down in his office.

14
00:00:55.060 --> 00:01:01.003
"ARGGGHHHHHHHH!" she suddenly cried, and stood up again.

15
00:01:01.004 --> 00:01:04.903
"I’m sorry. Oh, it’s only Spiky my hedgehog."

16
00:01:04.904 --> 00:01:09.745
Dr. Dolittle smiled at the sleepy animal she had sat on.

17
00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:14.273
Most of his patients never came back.

18
00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:19.191
The more animals Dr. Dolittle had, the fewer patients he had.

19
00:01:19.192 --> 00:01:23.074
"We are running out of money, John," Sarah complained.

20
00:01:23.075 --> 00:01:27.654
"Money," Dr. Dolittle sighed. "What a headache!"

21
00:01:27.655 --> 00:01:34.088
"Well, we can’t live without money!" Sarah said angrily.

22
00:01:34.089 --> 00:01:39.146
Of all the pets he had, Dr. Dolittle’s favorites were Jip the dog,

23
00:01:39.147 --> 00:01:48.342
Gub-Gub the baby pig, Dab-Dab the duck, Too-Too the owl, and of course, his parrot Polynesia.

24
00:01:48.343 --> 00:01:53.881
"You are my best friends," he often told them.

25
00:01:53.882 --> 00:01:56.448
"Woof woof!" barked Jip.

26
00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:03.695
"Quack, quack, quack, quack, oink, oink, snort," Dab-Dab and Gub-Gub cried cheerfully.

27
00:02:03.696 --> 00:02:08.657
"GWAK! Polly wants a cracker!" Polynesia chirped.

28
00:02:08.658 --> 00:02:13.297
Too-Too watched silently from the bookcase.

29
00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:17.603
"I’m getting tired of this, John!" Sarah shouted one day.

30
00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.411
"No one wants to come here!

31
00:02:19.412 --> 00:02:21.602
They don’t like the animals!"

32
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:25.603
She waved her hands around.

33
00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:30.473
"But I like animals better than people," the doctor replied.

34
00:02:30.474 --> 00:02:35.932
"Well, without money you can’t feed them, or ME or YOURSELF!"

35
00:02:35.933 --> 00:02:41.491
With that, Sarah stomped out of the room.

36
00:02:41.492 --> 00:02:43.244
But Sarah was right.

37
00:02:43.245 --> 00:02:45.711
Soon they ran out of money.

38
00:02:45.712 --> 00:02:51.547
Dr. Dolittle had to sell his piano, so the mice had no place to live.

39
00:02:51.548 --> 00:02:58.409
"Don’t worry, you can live inside my sock drawer," the doctor said.

40
00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:02.205
Even Dr. Dolittle’s bedroom was filled with animals.

41
00:03:02.206 --> 00:03:04.768
But he didn’t mind sharing.

42
00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:10.080
"There, you’ll be safe and warm," he told the mice.

43
00:03:10.081 --> 00:03:14.390
Now the townspeople didn’t go to Dr. Dolittle anymore.

44
00:03:14.391 --> 00:03:18.366
They traveled to another town when they needed a doctor.

45
00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:22.248
The only friends he had left were his pets.

46
00:03:22.249 --> 00:03:30.345
"Money," Dr. Dolittle sighed. "What a headache!"

